    <!-- ===== Ads: Unity LevelPlay (docs/MONETIZATION.md) =====
         This file is laid out exactly as the capacitor:sync:after hook
         (node_modules/capacitor-levelplay-ads/scripts/levelplay-manifest.js)
         writes it. Every `cap sync ios` re-serialises the whole plist and drops
         these comments; the keys and values come back identical. So after a sync
         `git diff` should show ONLY lost comments: anything else (a new
         SKAdNetwork id, an ad-network app id) was added by the hook and must be
         understood before archiving. Restore the comments with git checkout.

         There is no AdMob app id key here, deliberately, and there must never
         be one again. Google terminated the AdMob publisher account this app
         used on 2026-08-18; scripts/check-no-google.mjs fails every sync and
         release chain if that key, or AdMob's SKAdNetwork id, comes back. (It
         matches the key's name anywhere in this file, comments included, which
         is why this comment does not spell it out.) -->
    <!-- The App Tracking Transparency prompt. Required: an app that links an ad
         SDK and asks for ATT without this key is rejected. package.json
         levelplay.userTrackingDescription carries the SAME sentence; the sync
         hook inserts that value only when this key is missing, so the two must
         stay identical or a fresh project ships whichever one got there first. -->
    <key>NSUserTrackingUsageDescription</key>
    <string>Allow tracking so the ads you see stay relevant. The game plays the same either way.</string>
